                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "This is frankly an incredible video game. It's a strong contender for my favorite game of all time. I always find myself coming back to it, year after year, while that isn't really the case with other games in the genre like minecraft or vintage story. There's something inherently extremely satisfying and immersive about the gameplay loop of surviving on some alien planet or in deep space, building or stealing a ship, and then losing it in a hail of gunfire somewhere along the way.\n\nI think it does something really unique amongst games in its genre, which is give you a reason to build things. There's genuine challenges to overcome, be they self made, part of a scenerio, or part of the vanilla \"progression\" with the factorum and such. And those challenges carry risks. You'll spend a lot of time building some rover or spaceship, and it's entirely possible something will go very wrong and it will end up a cloud of debris, forcing you to try again. Maybe you'll design a boarding pod to try to capture a ship, and have it fail over and over, making you rethink it and iterate on it until it works. It feels like there's always something to do even after you have your production set up. It's fun, and unique. Maybe you just feel like building something cool in creative, and you can absolutely do that too.\n\nThe game is flawed of course. The physics are janky. It starts to lag if you build anything too big or fancy, butting up against the infamous \"pcu limit\". There's no npcs without mods, so you feel alone in a world of derelicts unless you play with friends. Multiplayer suffers streaming and desync issues. And worst of all, keen software house is... not a great developer and only cares about releasing an endless tide of DLC packs for the game, which might be the only game they haven't abandoned. The stuff in the DLCs isn't bad but the fact they exist at all while there's longstanding bugs going back a decade feels pretty scummy.\n\nThat said I think they really caught lightning in a bottle with this game because it is a ton of fun and just, hits right despite its flaws. I very very highly recommend it. As for the dlcs? Wait for a sale. The mods? Absolutely fantastic. Go wild. Don't touch space engineers 2 with a 10 foot pole though.",
